## Project Context

**Project:** ai_launchpad
**Purpose:** Cursor workspace for HNI AI development. The checkout at `hni-ai-dev-standards/` is the standards library and the MCP farm that serves it (standards, business context, lint, delivery, Playwright) plus the management console.
**Status:** Active development

### Stack
- **Standards:** Markdown in `hni-ai-dev-standards/standards/`, served by the `hni-standards` MCP server
- **MCP servers:** Python 3.12, Docker, streamable HTTP (`mcp-standards` and sibling servers)
- **Console:** Next.js app in `hni-ai-dev-standards/console` (Entra / MSAL sign-in)
- **Infra:** Pulumi (TypeScript) in `hni-ai-dev-standards/infra`, Azure Container Apps
- **Pipeline:** Bitbucket Pipelines — `development` / `qa` / `production`

### Environments
| Environment | URL | Branch |
|---|---|---|
| Local MCP | http://localhost:8000/mcp (`hni-standards`) | local checkout |
| Dev console | https://bastion-dev.hnicorp.com | development |

### External Team Dependencies
- HNI VPN is required to reach the deployed dev environment
- Entra group membership is required for console sign-in (an Admin adds the account)

### Project-Specific Notes
- This workspace contains the standards library itself. Compliance checks still go through the `hni-standards` MCP server so answers stay aligned with the running server, not a remembered copy of the files.
- Local server: `docker compose up --build` in `hni-ai-dev-standards/mcp-standards`. It listens on `http://localhost:8000/mcp`.
- Active exceptions to REQUIRED standards, if any, live in `GOVERNANCE-WAIVERS.md` at the workspace root. NEVER-severity standards cannot be waived.
